      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Quantitative Development\"\n",
        "date: \"2026-05-07\"\n",
        "categories: [github, quarto, reproducibility, quantitative-development]\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Motivation\n",
        "\n",
        "A quantitative development portfolio should demonstrate more than results. It should show how research is implemented, versioned, documented, tested, and published.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Standard\n",
        "\n",
        "The page should include:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. a clear research agenda;\n",
        "2. reproducible examples;\n",
        "3. public-safe datasets or synthetic data;\n",
        "4. implementation notes;\n",
        "5. diagnostics and limitations;\n",
        "6. links to repositories or technical appendices.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Minimal reproducible example\n"
      ],
      "id": "1335fe5b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "\n",
        "rng = np.random.default_rng(123)\n",
        "\n",
        "df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"date\": pd.date_range(\"2025-01-01\", periods=100),\n",
        "    \"return\": rng.normal(0, 0.01, 100)\n",
        "})\n",
        "\n",
        "df.head()"
      ],
      "id": "e0808a44",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Interpretation\n",
        "\n",
        "The objective is to make technical credibility visible: code quality, reproducibility, and the ability to communicate complex methods clearly."
      ],
      "id": "f1375890"
    }
  ],
